Apple today seeded the first betas of iOS 27.3, iPadOS 27.3, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS Golden Gate</a> 27.3, tvOS 27.3, and watchOS 27.3. The new software comes two days after Apple released the betas for developers.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iOS-27.3-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071817" /><br/>
iOS 27.3 is a major update that adds <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/03/ios-27-3-safari/">a Vertical Tabs layout option</a> and Adaptive <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ios-dark-mode/">Dark Mode</a> for Safari. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI can do more in and across Apple's apps, and developers are now able to create actions for &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; to carry out.<br/>
<br/>
The redesigned Health app is now available with custom Insights and Longevity information, and the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> supports Reachability. There's a new Selfie Sing feature in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a>, plus changes to StandBy on non-Duo iPhones. A full list of what's new in the beta <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ios-27-3-beta-features/">can be found in our guide</a>.<br/>
<br/>
On the Apple Watch Series 12 and Ultra 4, Audio Intelligence features Live Rewind and &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; Recap are available for testing. Live Rewind creates a transcript of the last 15 seconds of speech, and &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; Recap offers a high-level summary of conversations throughout the day.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;macOS Golden Gate&zwnj; 27.3 has the same Safari features, and it brings Live Activities to Macs without a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a>.<br/>
<br/>
To get the new betas, you can sign up on <a href="https://beta.apple.com">Apple's beta testing website</a>. After you're signed up, the betas can be installed through the Software Update section in the Settings app on each device.<br/>
